# The MAINNET treasury's env file. Copy to .env.mainnet ON THE HOST and fill it in.
#
#   docker compose -p clutch-main-treasury --env-file .env.mainnet \
#     -f docker-compose.mainnet.treasury.yml up -d
#
# EVERY SECRET HERE MUST DIFFER FROM .env. This is not tidiness. TRON addresses are
# network-agnostic, so one DEPOSIT_MNEMONIC derives the SAME deposit addresses on Nile and on
# mainnet; two orchestrators with separate databases would then hand one address to two different
# users, and a depositor shown that address by the testnet app could send real USDT and have the
# mainnet service credit somebody else.
#
# Most of the file is generated for you, on the host, by:
#   ENV_FILE=.env.mainnet bash scripts/provision-treasury-secrets.sh
# It never overwrites and has no --force: replacing a mnemonic orphans every address already
# handed out, which on this network means real money with no way back.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOU MUST SET THESE. Provisioning aborts without the first one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A TRON MAINNET wallet YOU control, where swept USDT lands. Nothing in this stack can spend from
# it -- that is deliberate (readiness A4/A5), and it is why this is the only address that matters
# for custody. Do not reuse the testnet's.
CUSTODY_TRON_ADDRESS=

# TRON mainnet, not Nile. Required rather than defaulted, because a default that is wrong in this
# pair means watching the wrong token on the wrong network and crediting nothing.
TRONGRID_URL=https://api.trongrid.io

# USDT (TRC-20) on TRON mainnet. VERIFY THIS ON tronscan.org BEFORE SETTING IT -- the value below
# is what it is widely published as, and a wrong contract here watches a token nobody is sending.
USDT_CONTRACT=TR7NHqjeKQxGTCi8q8ZY4pL8otSzgjLj6t

# Issued by trongrid.io against an account; the free tier's rate limits are low enough to stall
# deposit polling. Can be the same key as the testnet's -- it is a quota, not a secret about money.
# TRONGRID_API_KEY=       <- put in by provisioning from the repo secret; an empty line here would be set twice

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Azure KMS mint authority, from the key ceremony. Its address is this chain's
# genesis-committed mint_authority, so nothing else can ever mint here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AZURE_TENANT_ID=
AZURE_CLIENT_ID=
AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=
AZURE_VAULT_URL=https://clutch-mint-vault-1.vault.azure.net
AZURE_KEY_NAME=clutch-mint-key-1
# Pinned, never "latest": a new key version would change the mint authority's address under the
# running service without anyone deciding that.
AZURE_KEY_VERSION=

# Not read by docker-compose.mainnet.treasury.yml, which sets APP_MINT_AUTHORITY_SECRET to empty.
# The line stays because provision-treasury-secrets.sh generates a 64-hex key for every name that is
# missing, and scripts/mainnet-treasury-up.sh refuses to start when this value is hex. A plaintext
# mint key does not belong in this file. Leave the placeholder as it is.
MINT_AUTHORITY_SECRET=unused-this-chain-signs-with-kms

# CORS for the deposit API. The mainnet app only.
MAINNET_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://app.clutchprotocol.io

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Limits. Env vars, NOT genesis. The two MINT CAPS can be changed later with set-mint-caps.yml (chain
# mainnet), the other five by hand; check-cap-invariants.sh must pass after either. These are readiness
# B4's decided mainnet set (decided 2026-09-17) with the $2.00 redemption fee the maintainer accepted on
# 2026-10-02: the relay charges 1.50 USDT per transfer, and the fee must cover the transfer maximum
# (2.00). See mainnet-readiness.md B4 for what each one bounds. set-gasfree-settings.yml (network
# mainnet) writes exactly these. A pilot that wants smaller mint caps lowers them afterwards.
# The payout side is the PILOT's, not B4's decided set (accepted 2026-10-04, B4 "Pilot limits"):
# MAX_REDEMPTION_CLT and PER_TX_PAYOUT_CAP_USDT are $50 (decided: $200) and PAYOUT_FLOAT_TARGET_USDT,
# further down, is $100 (decided: about $1,000). Raise the three together, only after A2 ships.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PER_TX_MINT_CAP_CLT=1000000000
DAILY_MINT_CAP_CLT=2000000000
MAX_REDEMPTION_CLT=50000000
PER_TX_PAYOUT_CAP_USDT=50000000
MIN_REDEMPTION_CLT=25000000
REDEMPTION_FEE_USDT=2000000
DAILY_PAYOUT_CAP_CLT=1000000000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED on the host by provision-treasury-secrets.sh. Leave blank; do not copy from .env.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DEPOSIT_MNEMONIC=        <- generated, never printed to a terminal or a log
# DEPOSIT_ACCOUNT_XPUB=    <- derived from it and checked against it on every run
# PAYOUT_FLOAT_ADDRESS=    <- the plain float at 2/0, read off the signer; the GasFree float derives from it
# SIGNER_TOKEN=
# TREASURY_INITIATOR_TOKEN=
# TREASURY_APPROVER_TOKEN=
# TREASURY_READONLY_TOKEN=
# TREASURY_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# ORCHESTRATOR_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# JWT_SECRET=              <- must equal MAINNET_JWT_SECRET from .env, so the mainnet hub's
#                             tokens are the ones this orchestrator trusts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YOURS, put in by hand on the host before the first start.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=       <- openssl rand -base64 48; keep a copy somewhere that is not this host. The nightly backup aborts without it, and the start refuses.
# BACKUP_REMOTE=           <- an rclone destination for the mainnet dumps, not the one in .env. Optional; without it the dumps stay on this disk. "Provision treasury secrets" writes one if the file has none: stage's remote plus /mainnet.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The GasFree rail. Mainnet has its own API key and its own fee reading (design §9, read on 2026-10-02):
# the Nile key answers "Apikey not found." here. Same names and rules as .env.example's block.
# The key pair comes from https://developer.gasfree.io/ and goes in THIS file only, never in .env.
# PROBE=gasfree (Inspect stage) signs its mainnet reads with the pair it finds here.
# Until GASFREE_NETWORK and the whole block below are set, do not start or recreate the mainnet
# tron-signer: it turns GasFree on from the key alone and refuses to start without the network.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Live mainnet fees on 2026-10-02: 1.50 USDT to activate and 1.50 per transfer; the maxima leave 33% room.
# TRANSFER_RAIL=gasfree
# GASFREE_NETWORK=mainnet
# GASFREE_API_URL=https://open.gasfree.io/tron
# Set GASFREE_API_KEY and GASFREE_API_SECRET only together with GASFREE_NETWORK: tron-signer turns
# GasFree on by the key alone and then refuses to start without the network, so check-cap-invariants.sh
# stops "Mainnet — start the treasury" while the key is set and the network is not.
# GASFREE_API_KEY=
# GASFREE_API_SECRET=
# GASFREE_SERVICE_PROVIDER=TLntW9Z59LYY5KEi9cmwk3PKjQga828ird
# GASFREE_ACTIVATE_FEE_MAX_USDT=2000000
# GASFREE_TRANSFER_FEE_MAX_USDT=2000000
# MIN_DEPOSIT_USDT=5000000
# Read on 2026-09-24 and again on 2026-10-02 (PROBE=gasfree); read again before switching on.
# GASFREE_EXPECTED_IMPLEMENTATION=a3b0edffa1b94e93d297dcc9b6860175e9b537ec
# GASFREE_EXPECTED_CONTROLLER_IMPLEMENTATION=c8b13e3104f8a2d6e915ac132bdeda7faaf84d7d
# PAYOUT_FLOAT_TARGET_USDT=100000000
